# Skill Surface — cursor-sdk seat

**Seat wall.** The IDE rule is pruned here: no skill picker, no Reload Window, no Customize session — lead duties. One obligation survives.

## Invariant

```
edit(cursor-plugins/ulg-ecosystem/{skills,commands,rules}/ ∨ census)
  ⇒ HOME="$(getent passwd "$(id -un)" | cut -d: -f6)" \
       scripts/cursor/install-ecosystem-plugin.sh --local-only
```

Bare `scripts/cursor/install-ecosystem-plugin.sh` exits 1 here: `REFUSED` from `dispatch_home_host_guard` (overlay HOME). The prefix above is the run; `--local-only` skips Glass dest rsync. Copies land in `~/.cursor/plugins/local/ulg-ecosystem/`. `¬install ⇒ landed, not live`. Do not hand-copy.

| SoT path you touched | Install required? |
|---|---|
| `cursor-plugins/ulg-ecosystem/{skills,commands}/` | **Yes** |
| `cursor-plugins/ulg-ecosystem/rules/*_ulg.mdc` (+ `RULES_ULG_CENSUS`) | **Yes** |
| `{repo}/.cursor/skills/` or `*_ws.mdc` | No — checkout-local, read live |
| `cursor-plugins/ulg-ecosystem-seats/` | No — read from SoT at dispatch setup |

**Not yours.** Claude-slug bundle regeneration and Customize upload, `SKILLS_CENSUS` membership decisions, picker-staleness notes: do not attempt — name it in the closeout and let the lead route it.

**Skill bodies.** Say `Use the `{slug}` skill` and let the harness fetch it. Do **not** `fs`-read a `SKILL.md` into context to "load" a skill — that is the authoring path, and it burns the budget the skill layer exists to save.
